    "body": "It seems the situation is more complicated than that. See the test at https://jsbin.com/qeguwiy/edit?html,output. (Note also that [the rendering section](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#the-textarea-element-2) explicitly states white-space is supposed to apply.)\r\n\r\nPerhaps the simplest fix is indeed what you suggest, coupled with an attribute selector to switch it to white-space: pre when wrap=\"off\" is specified? But it'd be a fairly big departure from existing browser semantics. Something intermediate would be something like having normal/pre-wrap/pre-line compute to \"pre-wrap\", and nowrap/pre compute to \"pre\". That way you can turn off wrapping via CSS at least.\r\n\r\nI haven't tested actual getComputedStyle() values in any case, which will be something we'll want to write web platform tests for.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
