    "created_at": "2020-04-26T07:59:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-26T07:59:09Z",
    "body": "> And I cannot figure out a usecase that author may want different whitespace behavior for <textarea>.\r\n\r\nI'm that author.\r\nThis is my use case: I want to display base64 data in a textarea. The data is on multiple lines of fixed character length (think e.g. 76 chars line length limit for MIME).\r\nI want to display that data as a continuous stream of characters, no matter the width of the textarea (because I find it more pleasant to the eye) and yet maintain the real whitespaces, so that a user can copy/paste elsewhere and get multiple lines (and not an incredibly long line).\r\n\r\nThe following example render differently in Firefox (where I get what I want) and Chrome.\r\nhttps://jsbin.com/komutekona/edit?html,output\r\n\r\nNotably I have to use `white-space: normal` and `word-spacing: -7px` together to get the behaviour I want. `word-spacing` is somewhat an hack because it depends on the font: ideally I'd use an hypotetical `white-space: no-spaces`",
    "author_association": "NONE",
